ications.</li>
    <li><strong>Architectures and tools:</strong> data collection/storage, processing/analysis, and tools/providers such as Hive, Pig and Flume.</li>
    <li><strong>Common applications:</strong> dashboards, storage-system solutions, processing systems and analytics systems.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud practical case:</strong> cloud architecture; IaaS/PaaS/SaaS; Azure, AWS and Google Cloud; PowerShell/scripting; virtual machines; components/architectures; cloud administration; end-to-end simple cloud application development; monitoring, optimisation and troubleshooting; cost planning and management.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Management, personal and social skills</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Identify when a Big Data system is appropriate and what advantages it offers.</li>
    <li>Critically evaluate Big Data service offerings.</li>
    <li>Develop and put into production a simple cloud Big Data system.</li>
    <li>Administer a cloud Big Data system responsibly.</li>
