  <h2 class="module">Training Module 4 — Fundamentals of Probability and Statistics with R</h2>
  <p><strong>Duration:</strong> 60 hours</p>
  <h3>Objective</h3>
  <p>Make predictions and analyse data to draw inferences from available information and support decision-making in health sciences.</p>
  <p class="footer">IFCD104 · Unofficial English translation for portfolio review</p>
</section>

<section class="page">
  <h2>Training Module 4 — Probability and Statistics with R</h2>
  <h3>Learning outcomes</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Scientific knowledge cycle:</strong> scientific method, experimental design, observation/data collection, mathematical/statistical methods, hypotheses and models.</li>
    <li><strong>Descriptive statistics:</strong> frequency tables and graphical representations including pie charts, bar charts, histograms and frequency polygons.</li>
    <li><strong>Statistical parameters:</strong> central tendency, dispersion, skewness and shape.</li>
    <li><strong>Exploratory graphics:</strong> qualitative, discrete quantitative and continuous quantitative data.</li>
    <li><strong>Probability:</strong> definitions and properties, Laplace's rule, combinatorics and Bayes' theorem.</li>
    <li><strong>Random variables:</strong> discrete and continuous variables, expected value, variance and standard deviation.</li>
    <li><strong>Distributions:</strong> binomial and normal distributions.</li>
    <li><strong>Hypothesis testing:</strong> significance tests/limits, Type I and Type II errors, alpha and beta risks.</li>
    <li><strong>Biomedical Big Data:</strong> personal medical data, anonymisation, data-protection legislation and biomedical data types.</li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Management, personal and social skills</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Identify the origin and type of biomedical-computing data.</li>
    <li>Prepare rigorous reports and visualisations.</li>
    <li>Justify conclusions and predictions from healthcare statistical studies.</li>
    <li>Manage and exploit large healthcare databases responsibly.</li>
  </ul>
  <p class="footer">IFCD104 · Unofficial English translation for portfolio review</p>
</section>

